red to the Pathology Fine  Needle Aspiration Biopsy Service by Michelle Specht  MD for consultation and  diagnosis of a lesion in the right breast mass     Clinical History  Patient on Coumadin for Factor V Leiden  large right breast  mass at 10 00 o clock     Physical Exam  The right breast showed a 4cm non tender ill defined   irregular  firm and fixed mass at 10 00 o clock     Assessment  Based on the clinical history and physical examination  an FNAB is  warranted     Procedure  The procedure and potential complications were explained to the  patient  who understood the purpose  risks  and benefits of the procedure  The  patient confirmed name  date of birth  laterality  and lesion to be aspirated   Written consent was obtained     The biopsy procedure was performed by palpation     5 aspirates were performed using 23 gauge needles with local anesthesia and  without complications   3 slides were stained for immediate evaluation     The procedure was performed by Elena Brachtel  M D     Disposition  The immediate interpretation findings not discussed with the  patient  Michelle Specht  MD was notified of the preliminary results by personal  communication at 3 20 p m         The signing pathologist attests that he she performed the procedure or  if  performed by a resident or fellow  directed and supervised the FNA procedure and  was immediately available to further assist the resident fellow before  during  and after the procedure  and has reviewed and confirmed the interpretation of  slides stained for immediate evaluation            Electronically Signed Out By  Elena F  Brachtel MD on REMOVED_DATE 17 27       Hormone Receptor Quantitation  Ordered Date  REMOVED_DATE    B  BREAST CELLBLOCK  RIGHT   Block tested   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   The invasive tumor cells do not stain for estrogen receptor protein   The invasive tumor cells do not stain for progesterone receptor protein   The invasive tumor cells show strong  3   overexpression of HER 2 protein       Note 