Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final  Type  Cytology  Cytology Report  ML 10  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   CASE  ML 10  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME   Date Taken  REMOVED_DATE Source Care Unit  FNAB Clinic  ACC 270  Resident   Reports To   JENNIFER BELMONTE  PA        FINE NEEDLE ASPIRATION BIOPSY SERVICE   PATIENT EVALUATION    Chief Complaint  This 54 year old female was referred to the fine needle  aspiration clinic by Jennifer Belmonte  PA for consultation and diagnosis of a  right breast lump     Clinical History  Patient noticed a right breast lump for one week     Review of Symptoms   Constitutional  None     Social History  Married with two children     Family History  Sister had breast and lung cancer     Review of Patient Data   Radiology  ultrasound and mammogram show suspicious mass  1 1cm   at 2 o clock  in right breast   Office Notes  Reviewed     Physical Examination  Laterality was established according to departmental  protocol  Examination of the right breast reveals a poorly defined  fixed  firm  nodule measuring 1cm  located at 2 o clock close to the midline of chest wall     Assessment  Based on the clinical history and physical examination  an FNAB is  warranted     Procedure  The procedure and complications were explained to the patient and  consent was obtained  2 aspirates were performed using 23 gauge needles  without anesthesia and without complications  2 slides were stained for  immediate evaluation  additional tissue was submitted for further evaluation   See corresponding cytology report MN 10  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID      Rapid Interpretation  Positive for carcinoma     Disposition  The immediate interpretation findings were discussed with the  patient  The preliminary results were communicated to Jennifer Belmonte  PA by  Dr  Shen at 2 30 p m       Final Diagnosis by Jian Shen M D   Ph D   Electronically signed on Thursday  REMOVED_MONTH 28   REMOVED_CASE_ID  at 12 52 47PM  By his her signature above  the pathologist listed as making the Final  Diagnosis certifies that he she has personally reviewed this case and confirmed  or corrected the diagnoses     Specimen  Patient Evaluation  T  Management  Specimen   see also MN 10  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  of corresponding FNAB        report_end  , Absent.
